line  start window   clip tempo  text
   0   3.90   3.88   2.54  1.00  Look, it's raining! Where does rain come from?
   1   7.83   4.97   3.42  1.00  I know! A giant up in the sky has a big watering can!
   2  12.85   6.17   4.82  1.00  Good guess, Leo! What a funny idea. But rain comes from... the clouds!
   3  19.07   3.96   2.81  1.00  From the clouds? But how does the water get up there?
   4  23.08   4.77   3.82  1.00  Let's follow one tiny drop of water. Meet Drippy!
   5  27.90   5.12   3.37  1.00  Hi! I'm Drippy the raindrop! Come on an adventure with me!
   6  33.07   4.29   2.94  1.00  Question one. How does Drippy get up into the sky?
   7  37.41   5.63   4.48  1.00  I'm in the big blue sea. The warm sun shines on me. Ooh, I feel warm!
   8  43.09   4.85   3.30  1.00  I get so light, I float up, up, up! You can't see me now!
   9  47.99   4.90   2.15  1.00  Point up with Drippy! Up, up, up!
  10  52.94   6.14   4.79  1.00  High in the sky, it's cold! Brrr! I turn back into a tiny drop.
  11  59.13   5.71   3.56  1.00  And look! Lots of tiny drops, all together. We make a cloud!
  12  64.89   3.95   2.60  1.00  Question two. Why does rain fall down?
  13  68.89   6.40   5.05  1.00  Inside the cloud, the tiny drops bump into each other, and join together.
  14  75.34   4.42   2.67  1.00  Bump! I get bigger. Bump! Bigger! Bump! Bigger!
  15  79.81   5.03   2.28  1.00  Say it with Drippy! Bump! Bigger!
  16  84.89   5.14   3.99  1.00  When the drops get big and heavy, the cloud can't hold them anymore.
  17  90.08   4.27   1.92  1.00  Whoa! Here I go! Wheee! I'm rain!
  18  94.40   3.61   2.26  1.00  Question three. Where does the rain go?
  19  98.06   4.86   3.51  1.00  Splash! I land on a hill, and I slide down into a river.
  20 102.97   5.60   4.05  1.00  Some raindrops help the flowers and trees drink, and grow.
  21 108.62   3.96   2.41  1.00  The river takes me all the way back to the sea!
  22 112.63   5.82   4.48  1.00  And then the sun warms the water again, and up, up, up it goes!
  23 118.50   7.23   5.88  1.00  Up, cloud, rain, and back to the sea. Round and round! This is called the water cycle.
  24 125.78   4.62   1.87  1.00  Wa-ter cy-cle! Your turn!
  25 130.45   4.63   3.28  1.00  Whoa! So rain is the same water, going round and round!
  26 135.13   6.46   4.31  1.00  Yes! The water in your bath was in a cloud, long, long ago!
  27 141.64   4.63   3.28  1.00  We can make rain in a jar! Ask a grown-up to help.
  28 146.32   5.50   3.75  1.00  Step one. A grown-up pours warm water into a jar.
  29 151.87   5.23   3.48  1.00  Step two. Put a plate on top, with ice cubes on it.
  30 157.15   5.51   1.96  1.00  Now, wait, and watch.
  31 162.71   7.26   5.31  1.00  Look! Tiny drops under the cold plate. They get bigger, and... drip, drip! Rain!
  32 170.02   3.96   1.61  1.00  We made rain! Hooray!
  33 174.03   3.67   2.72  1.00  Prof. Hoot, are raindrops pointy, like this?
  34 177.75   7.28   5.93  1.00  Good question! Real raindrops are not pointy. Small ones are round, like little balls.
  35 185.08   5.15   3.60  1.00  And big ones look a bit like a tiny bun! Wow!
  36 190.28   3.88   1.53  1.00  A bun? Now I'm hungry!
  37 194.21   4.08   2.53  1.00  Look! The sun is back. And... a rainbow!
  38 198.34   5.58   4.03  1.00  When sunshine shines through the raindrops, it makes a rainbow!
  39 203.97   5.25   2.90  1.00  Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple!
  40 209.27   3.27   1.12  1.00  Thank you, rain!
  41 212.59   2.42   1.27  1.00  Let's remember!
  42 215.06   6.35   1.40  1.00  Where does rain come from?
  43 221.46   3.10   1.15  1.00  From the clouds!
  44 224.61   6.97   2.02  1.00  What makes the water go up into the sky?
  45 231.63   3.14   1.19  1.00  The warm sun!
  46 234.82   6.65   1.70  1.00  Why do the drops fall down?
  47 241.52   3.78   1.83  1.00  They get big and heavy!
  48 245.35   6.73   1.78  1.00  Where does the river take Drippy?
  49 252.13   2.99   1.04  1.00  Back to the sea!
  50 255.17   7.87   2.91  1.00  What do we call it, when water goes round and round?
  51 263.09   3.29   1.34  1.00  The water cycle!
  52 266.43   7.91   2.96  1.00  What do we see, when the sun shines through raindrops?
  53 274.39   2.97   1.02  1.00  A rainbow!
  54 277.41   2.57   1.72  1.00  Let's say it all together!
  55 280.03   2.02   1.17  1.00  Up, up, up!
  56 282.10   1.63   0.78  1.00  Cloud!
  57 283.78   1.53   0.68  1.00  Rain!
  58 285.36   2.95   1.40  1.00  And round again!
  59 288.36   6.16   3.21  1.00  Your turn! Up, up, up! Cloud! Rain! And round again!
  60 294.57   3.59   2.64  1.00  Thanks for coming on my adventure! Bye-bye!
  61 298.21   6.44   1.75  1.00  See you next time, friends!
